      "worked": "By symmetry, choosing all except one object is equivalent to choosing the one object to leave out, so $\\binom{n}{n-1}=\\binom{n}{1}=n$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\binom{100}{99}\\binom{99}{98}&=\\binom{100}{1}\\binom{99}{1}\\\\\n\\binom{100}{99}\\binom{99}{98}&=100\\times99\\\\\n\\binom{100}{99}\\binom{99}{98}&=100(100-1)\\\\\n\\binom{100}{99}\\binom{99}{98}&=9900.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
